#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# nest_while_list

#% text
# `nest_while_list(f, x, test)` gives the list of the values `nest_while(f, x, test)` goes through, from `x` to the first value for which `test` fails.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `nest_while_list(f, x, test, 1, max)` applies `f` at most `max` times.

#% item
# The list always starts with `x`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
nest_while_list(n => n/2, 96, is_even)
#% output
#= [96, 48, 24, 12, 6, 3]

#% subsection
# Applications

#% text
# A Collatz sequence until it reaches 1:

#% cell
nest_while_list(n => if is_even(n) then n/2 else 3n + 1, 7, n => n != 1)
#% output
#= [7, 22, 11, 34, 17, 52, 26, 13, 40, 20, 10, 5, 16, 8, 4, 2, 1]

#% subsection
# Properties and relations

#% text
# `nest_list` takes a fixed number of steps instead:

#% cell
nest_list(n => n/2, 96, 3)
#% output
#= [96, 48, 24, 12]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `nest_while`, `nest_list`, `fixed_point_list`
